message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below. 若使用本作，请按下述格式引用。"
type: book
title: "只能选两样：从来不及、会忘记到说不清——六个核心，看懂复杂世界的取舍 / Pick Two: Six Ideas for Understanding a Complicated World"
abstract: >-
  本著作是这一系列的入口读本：用六个核心，把六本学术专著写成一本从十岁到专家都能读完的书。 核心主张：看得见的世界背后有一张看不见的账单，账单只有三个价格——看得准、拼得上、传得下去，最多付得起两个。六个核心（看见、记住、跟上、选择、讲述、临界）就是学会读这六张账单。 结构与证据：19 部、123 页、29 幅图；四种读者分层（故事／多想一层／再想一层／给专家的注），每部配三个生活故事与动手练习，另有练习册、常见误解、给老师家长的一页与二十五个真实的人。 诚实的纪律：每个核心都标明对应专著的证据等级；凡通俗化损伤原意之处，以专著为准；本书不新增实证结论。 边界：它是入口，不是替代；具体结论与失败记录在六本专著中。它同时是系列的外部登记库（最小可验证单元、跨域盲测登记、合并术语表）。 版本：2026-10-25，123 页，19 部，29 图；源码开源，内容 CC BY 4.0，代码 MIT。
  Abstract (English). This is the entry volume of the series: six core ideas turn six monographs into a book readable from age ten to specialist. Core thesis: behind the visible world lies an invisible bill with three prices — being precise, fitting together, and carrying over — and at most two can be paid; the six cores (seeing, remembering, keeping up, choosing, telling, criticality) teach how to read that bill. Structure and evidence: 19 parts, 123 pages, 29 figures; four reader levels (story / one layer deeper / one more / expert note), three short stories and a hands-on exercise per part, plus a workbook, common misconceptions, a page for teachers and parents, and twenty-five real people. Discipline: each core points to the evidence grade of its source monograph; where popularisation distorts the original, the monograph prevails; the book adds no new empirical claims. Boundaries: it is an entry point, not a substitute; it also serves as the series' external registry. Edition: 2026-10-25, 123 pages, 19 parts, 29 figures. This edition unifies the “part” numbering across TOC/EPUB/Markdown, converts straight quotes to Chinese quotation marks, removes duplicated nested callouts, corrects the opening title to “four small things, three sentences”, syncs the actual counts of Parts 7/10/12/14, updates the series page to nine books, and corrects the DOI of The Price of Choice.
